From: Shane de Deuge <shane@scielex.com.au>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mangoh-yellow: WL_REG_ON on GPIO33 for DV3 boards

DV3 boards have WL_REG_ON on WP GPIO33 where later boards have it on the SX1509 expander. Applied
only with MANGOH_YELLOW_REV = "dv3". Not yet tried on a DV3 board.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board specific]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/swi-wp-mangoh-yellow.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/swi-wp-mangoh-yellow.dtsi
@@ -154,7 +154,8 @@
 		/* matches the qcom,vdd-voltage-level set for sdhc_2 in mdm9607-wp76xx.dtsi */
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <2850000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <2850000>;
-		gpio = <&sx1509 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		/* DV3 boards: WL_REG_ON is on WP GPIO33 (TLMM 78), not the expander */
+		gpio = <&tlmm_pinmux 78 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		enable-active-high;
 		/* the old script waited 2 s after WL_REG_ON; the chip needs well under that */
 		startup-delay-us = <250000>;
